<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">United Malays National Organisation</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1946–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as UMNO</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The United <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malays">Malays</a> National Organisation (UMNO) is a Malay nationalist party founded in 1946 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/onn-jaafar">Onn Jaafar</a> to oppose the British Malayan Union plan. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunku-abdul-rahman">Tunku Abdul Rahman</a> it formed the Alliance with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaysian-chinese-association">Malayan Chinese Association</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaysian-indian-congress">Malayan Indian Congress</a>, which won the 1955 election and led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaya">Malaya</a> to independence in 1957. Through the Alliance and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barisan-nasional">Barisan Nasional</a> it governed Malaysia without interruption until its defeat in 2018.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-malays-national-organisation.jpg" alt="United Malays National Organisation" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original work from UMNO; retrieved by 白布飘扬 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:UMNO_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
